Package: libomxdsp-dev
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libomx-contract-dev (>= 3.9.0~), libomx-contract-dev (<< 4~), omx-dsp-contract (= ${source:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: audio toolbox of the OpenMixer console, a real-time-safe C library
 libomxdsp is the sound of the OpenMixer console, as a library: the filters,
 envelopes, delays, limiters, gates, compressors and other building blocks of
 a mixer channel, written in plain C that never allocates, locks or calls the
 system while audio is running. The console and the omx plugins are built from
 this same code, so an effect sounds the same on the desk and in your DAW,
 sample for sample. Link it into your own plugin, effect or audio tool and
 start from parts that are already tested against exact results at every
 sample rate.
 .
 This package holds the headers and the static library in three flavours,
 each with its pkg-config file: libomxdsp.a (omxdsp), libomxdsp-contracts.a
 (omxdsp-contracts, contracts compiled in) and libomxdsp-tsan.a (omxdsp-tsan,
 contracts and ThreadSanitizer). Programs link the library statically; no
 shared library exists.
 .
 Its documentation is on openmixer.org.

Package: omx-rt-gate
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: libomxdsp-dev (= ${binary:Version}), gcc, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: static real-time gate for plugin and engine C built on libomxdsp
 omx-rt-gate proves that the real-time code of a plugin or an audio engine
 never allocates, locks, sleeps, does I/O or logs. It compiles each real-time
 source with the project's own flags, reads the compiler's call graph, finds
 the functions a host calls from its audio thread in the plugin's LV2, CLAP or
 PipeWire tables, and follows every call from there, through libomxdsp's own
 code too. Each finding names the call, its place and the path from the entry
 point. The tables it judges against ship with it: one forbidden list, one
 class table and the thread roles of each ABI, with libomxdsp's thread tags
 and call graphs.
 .
 Its documentation is on openmixer.org.

Package: omx-dsp-contract
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: omx-contract-data (>= 3.9.0~), omx-contract-data (<< 4~), ${misc:Depends}
Breaks: libomxdsp-dev (<< ${source:Version})
Replaces: libomxdsp-dev (<< ${source:Version})
Description: omx-dsp's kernel and instance declarations, read at run time
 omx-dsp's package of omx-contract's contract directory: the declarations of
 its kernels and instance faces (their controls, units and readouts) under
 /usr/share/omx-contract/contract.d/3/omx-dsp. A program that reads them while
 it runs (a panel, the omx-contract command) needs this package, not the
 development one.
 .
 Its documentation is on openmixer.org.
